      "updated_at": "2025-10-19T14:31:33Z",
      "body": "Also if you want a full coverage of ssl + hashlib modules, you need to build both OpenSSL 3.5 and OpenSSL 1.1.1 from sources with M/ASan because some code paths are conditioned to the OpenSSL version.\n\nMore generally, linked librairies must he built with the corresponding sanitizers (so this includes at least ncurses and openssl for CPython, as well as all the compression libs which I do not remember the name of)",
